+---
+timestamp: 2026-08-13T00:00:00Z
+title: fix-claude-tmux-ready-detector — gem packaging + version-tolerant ready detection
+---
+
+- **Packaging fix:** `hive.gemspec` now globs `lib/hive/scripts/**/*` so a clean `gem install` ships `interactive_claude_wrapper.sh` and `stop_hook.sh` (previously only `lib/**/*.rb` shipped, silently breaking tmux-mode launcher and the Stop hook). New `Hive::PackagedScripts` is the single source of truth for every runtime-invoked script; `ClaudeLauncher.wrapper_command` and `StopHookInstaller` reference it now. Guarded by an extended `gemspec_test` unit check plus a new built-gem integration test (`test/integration/packaged_gem_test.rb`) and a `packaging/check_packaged_scripts.rb` gate wired into `release.yml`.
+- **Detector fix:** `Hive::ClaudeLauncher` now accepts a Unicode separator / NBSP (U+00A0) after `❯` (Claude Code 2.1.179 renders a non-breaking space) and scans the last ~10 nonblank lines of the input-box tail instead of a fixed 2-line/footer offset, so the separator/caret/separator/footer shape reads as ready. Menu-option / permission / trust rejections are unchanged. Regression fixtures under `test/fixtures/panes/claude_*_2_1_179.txt` lock the 2.1.179 shapes. See [[gaps]] for the residual version-coupled positive-marker risk and the out-of-scope daemon binary-drift e2e note.
